  :seon.task/plan "DONE SLICE (runtime-2, 2026-11-15): root boots by load-diff. seon.program/load-all! {:tests? false} at root's boot (after hold-config!, before the fork server is forked) reads live-ids first, rows only for forms whose ids the binary lacks, and unmaps the binary's definitions main dropped (bin/build records them as binary-program's :defs, seon.program/defined-keys), only in namespaces main holds; the spawn refusal on a stale binary is deleted (docs/source.md#a-boot-runs-mains-program; proofs seon.program-test/a-process-on-another-program-unmaps-what-main-dropped-and-loads-what-it-changed, seon.system-test/a-root-on-a-binary-of-another-program-runs-mains-program). NEXT SLICE: stale-binary, its row, the ROOT STALE BINARY line and booted-source's withheld inputs stay while a build input (pins, deps.edn, native) is the binary's and not main's; they go once root's start asks deps' seon.fx/runtime-for as an agent's does (bin/system builds on that line today). The fork server then takes the same ids-first path (it re-reads every live row and re-evaluates what root loaded). The runtime invariant (owner, 2026-11-11: a process runs its branch's program; docs/merging.md#a-session-proves-through-root). Owner: runtime. What exists [M, HEAD 6184c92521]: the oracle, seon.program/program-differs (program.clj:1466, over diff-plan :1419), and seon.program/loaded (each var's form id this process last evaluated); seon.agent/run-tests-forked refuses with :seon.agent/program-differs before its first item (proved by seon.source-test/a-process-that-runs-another-program-than-its-branch-is-told-so); an agent names the program it holds as a reference {:seon.db/branch :commit :t} set at its start (seon.agent/program-db, agent.clj:262, 6184c92521) and a test child brings itself to the branch by load-diff! from it (agent.clj:1316-1317); load-diff! (program.clj:1497) removes what the target lacks and loads what it adds. Four loaders still compute what changed: load-all! (:1380; the fork server's boot and first fork, fork_server.clj:155/210/354), load-diff! (spawn, resume, test child), load-changes! (:1514; root's writer writer.clj:45, the fork server's :tx fork_server.clj:197, an agent's merge-main! agent.clj:587), reload-dependents! (:1484, an eval's macro dependents). Cause: no one start: each caller decides how its process reaches its program. Design (ruling 2026-11-14, one start): every process starts through one act: deps' seon.fx/runtime-for (binary identity: a digest of build inputs vs target/seon's) routes to a binary of the right digest, then seon.program/load-diff! from the binary's recorded forms (or the forker's db) to the reference's db; the process's :program is that reference; nothing downstream re-checks (principle 5: bootstrap once). A later move of the branch is the program reaction (one derivation), the same load-diff! from the held reference. Interface (owner, 2026-11-11: \"seon.test/prove #commit id ... and that runs it\"): (seon.system/prove! sys ref) and (... ref names); a ref at a past :t or :commit always forks. Deletes, with the one start: load-all! (the boot is load-diff! from the binary's forms), load-changes! (the reaction), binary-current's reach check, judged-path, seon.problems/stale-binary and bin/check's tree compare; class 3 readers of baked values (seon.db/schema and schema-digest db.clj:15/24, seon.config/keys-declared) then read the held reference's value or are named main-only. Never removes functionality: each caller moves to the start or the reaction. Estimate: load-diff! costs the diff (diff-plan reads only differing datoms) plus ~2.5M ticks a changed form (measured, eval-cache share); a whole load of 5,676 forms was 134 s, 7.6B ticks (2026-11-11), so the far-back replay only. Proofs, red first: seon.source-test/a-process-that-runs-another-program-than-its-branch-is-told-so (exists); seon.program-test/a-branch-narrowing-a-schema-and-a-config-default-proves-red-by-the-one-call; seon.program-test/a-reference-at-an-earlier-commit-runs-that-commits-program; design guard seon.main-test/a-program-loads-only-through-the-one-start (no caller of a seon.program loader outside the start and the reaction: principle 5's owed law). PART 2 SPLIT (agreed deps and runtime-2, 2026-11-15 ~06:55): deps does (1) root's start asks seon.fx/runtime-for, through the :git effect or bin/system start's inputs, never git in root's process; stale-binary becomes a digest mismatch only, its row and the ROOT STALE BINARY line kept for that case, booted-source's withheld inputs go; (2) seon.system/prove-tree!'s tree refusal (fx.clj ~593) asks runtime-for; baked-changes, build-input?'s hand list (system.edn stays) and judged-path go. Out of it: bin/test's and bin/check's binary-current rule (tests). (3) A resumed branch whose :seon.system/source is behind main's runtime merges main first, or its env-mismatch says to (Stage 0, 2026-11-15: lb76's spawn was refused until root merged main into it; context attached at 06:46 after the merge [M]). Evidence of the two-identities class [M, deps run22 06:43]: bin/prove's binary-current (by reach) said target/seon was current while runtime-for (by digest) refused the same tree in seon.system-test/a-second-boot-resumes-the-same-main, the on-disk tree having moved (a fork checkout committed mid-prove): one identity, computed once at the one start, removes both. INTERFACE AGREED (deps and runtime-2, root approved, 2026-11-15): the one binary identity is seon.fx/runtime-for. (runtime-for tree) or (runtime-for tree {:scope :all}) answers {:binary path :digest d} when the binary is current for tree (with :all also :program, the src tree id, for a process whose store holds no Seon program and so runs the baked one), else the typed :seon.process/env-mismatch carrying :seon.process/binary-digest, :seon.process/branch-digest, :seon.process/tree and :seon.process/differs (the build inputs or pins that differ, as paths). The answer is kept by tree id (a tree is immutable): that kept value is the ONE value every reader takes. Every start asks it: root's boot, an agent's start, a test child's fork. The restart predicate (seon.system/a-landing-restarts-root-only-for-a-binary-change) is exactly (contract/error? (runtime-for main-tree)) plus no agent mid-turn, and bin/update's restart line prints :seon.process/differs; neither keeps a second cache. seon.system/binary-current, baked-changes, build-input?'s list, judged-path and stale-binary's tree compare are deleted (measured on root, result/af121268: runtime-for 4.8k ticks says current, binary-current 272M ticks and 1.3 GB says stale for src root already load-diffs). Plan: notes/deps-part2-one-binary-identity-plan-2026-11-15.md. DELETION SPLIT (deps and runtime-2, 2026-11-15, so system.clj is never edited by both at once): runtime-2's G landing deletes restart-for and loads-in-place? (held-inputs and runs/root-inputs.edn stay: booted-source puts them on root's source fact, and agents key their test results by them, agent.clj:838, 925, main.clj:182, test_runner.clj:725; runtime-2's correction, 2026-11-15) and reads (runtime-for main-tree) plus no agent mid-turn; deps' landing right after it, from main, deletes seon.system/binary-current, baked-changes, build-input?'s list, judged-path and stale-binary's tree compare, keeping booted-source's :inputs path as it is, moving their callers to seon.fx/runtime-for (boot's stale row; test_runner's :all build decision and bin/check with tests-4). runtime-for's half (kept by tree id, :seon.process/differs, {:scope :all}) is c9cf4ae5c3 on jolt/deps, landing with deps' Jolt pin 62476381. Deps reviewed G SLICE: approved; add a proof that an at-load config line's change restarts. PART 2 AS RULED (root, 2026-11-15 16:4x; urgent after deps' items 3+4 pin), from today's two cases [M]: (a) 15:53 spawns refused while update kept running: an untracked clone (reference-code/core.async-flow) in the main checkout entered bin/tree's working tree as a gitlink, so a build's identity (25fd5003) differed from main's committed one (c7311e6b) while binary-current, comparing committed trees, said current; tests-4's 199 false reds the same day. (b) 16:36 a false mismatch: bin/binary-digest's waiting() finds at-load keys by a line regex '^ :seon.config...', which never sees a schema file's FIRST entry (it starts with '{'); 88bfdca896 put :seon.config.render/flush-max first in seon.config.render.edn, so the at-load token-budget moved to second, entered the digest, and c7311e6b became 76dc758d with no real change; the worse half, a first-in-file at-load key has never been in the identity (a silent miss). FIXES: (1) a pin is a gitlink named in .gitmodules, never an untracked nested repo (bin/binary-digest and the tree it digests); (1b) the at-load and place keys come from the schema DATA (the binary's registry through a thin seon mode), never a regex over EDN text (the no-parsing-composed-text rule); (2) bin/update's keep-or-restart asks runtime-for, the same check as spawn: 'not current' is the restart, never 'kept running'; (3) runtime-for compares the RUNNING process's build (its digest held at boot), not whatever target/seon a later build left; plus binary-current, baked-changes, build-input?, elsewhere? and judged-path deleted, their callers on runtime-for (test_runner.clj:383 and :797 by deps, tests-4 reviewing; seon.system/stale-binary; prove-tree!; bin/check:86-94). Proofs, red first on today's real cases: the first-entry at-load key (token-budget) is in the digest wherever its entry sits; an untracked nested repo moves no digest; update restarts when runtime-for says not current; an env-mismatch keeps both digests on the agent's record."
