 {:seon.task/name "a-tests-digest-reads-what-it-ran"
  :seon.task/plan "Owners: runtime (the outside reads: code, config, files, pins as recorded keys, with data; plan Stage 1.5), tests (verdicts and reuse), context (status reads), web (digests across a merge and a rebase). Owner, 2026-11-08: \"I don't understand how we don't know what tests ran? That sounds like a bug.\"; 2026-11-07: \"I want a tests digest to be the inputs (ideally just a seed) so yeah there is no need to rerun them if the seed is the same and so are the functions.\" What exists [M]: a test's digest is static: its reach plus the input classes its reached forms name (seon.program/graph-index, program.clj:2259; reach-graph :2047); seon.profile/reads records each contracted function a run called (in each verdict's :fns since 813786f9db, 7 ticks a counted call). Seen: a process test's verdict misses code it runs in processes it boots or drives by text (seon.system-test/a-second-boot-in-one-process-is-refused reused old greens; a forced red at a green's digest read FLAKY); Scheme text in seon.profile changed with no digest move (2026-11-10). Cause: the static reach cannot follow messages to a server or text sent to another process. Design (one derivation, agreed 2026-11-14 with conditions): a run records what it read as datom keys (Datahike's read recorder) plus outside reads (each var's loaded form digest once per var per run, as a set, never per call; config keys at seon.config/resolve-in; files; the pin), each booted or driven process reporting its own reads into the verdict; a green stands while every recorded read is unchanged; a test with no recorded reads runs (never skipped), and new code's first run is the default; the static reach graph retires only after that holds. A reaction's re-run is work: it runs as an effect on the effects owner's :process kind with its declared bound, admitted from the cores. Deletes, once a fresh empty-cache full run on main finds no false green: the static reach graph as the reuse key, seon.program's registry-walker rule, and the hand-kept quoted symbol lists in seon.agent-test (five tests). Estimate: recorder cost one set conj per distinct var per run; 1M calls cost ~1M x 15 ticks only if not deduped at the call site, so dedupe is required [H]. Proofs, red first: seon.program-test/test-process-ran-code-through-string-sent-root; seon.program-test/a-million-calls-record-each-var-once (held to its estimate); seon.proofs-test/a-test-with-no-recorded-reads-runs."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.program-test/test-process-ran-code-through-string-sent-root seon.program-test/a-million-calls-record-each-var-once seon.proofs-test/a-test-with-no-recorded-reads-runs}}
