 {:seon.task/name "a-metric-accretes"
  :seon.task/plan "Not ready. State 2026-11-11: step (1) is decided: the metric's per-function sum is no longer written (it was 30-77% of what an agent branch wrote, measured on the standing root, and two branches rewrote one entity's one attribute, which a merge of everything would conflict on; the owner's ruling that no such value is stored, Point's ruling for the deletion). What exists: each agent's process measures live, (:fn-costs @seon.agent/state) (docs/sharing.md#a-functions-cost-is-a-fact; seon.agent-test/what-a-function-cost-is-measured-live-and-never-stored). Left, when something reads costs across runs and agents (the measures work with Tests): each run's measure as its own fact a merge unions (an entity per function, form digest, agent and run, by content identity), the total a render, never a stored sum; then (2) a test's verdict :fns and :seon.eval/fns are the same data in other shapes, folded into it or said why not; (3) root and the fork server, which count but never write; (5) a derived health class over it, its bound from the population. The :seon.fn/* schema entries leave the store at its next erase. Proofs exist: seon.profile-test/stats-add-the-same-however-they-were-split."
