 {:seon.task/name "a-pin-reruns-only-the-tests-its-library-forms-reach"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: deps, the library half of tests-4's landing 12 (recorded reads decide reruns); root 2026-11-15. Measured first and a graph design dropped [M, root REPL, main's reach graph, 2,128 tests]: 1,413 Seon forms name a datahike var; 1,574 tests reach datahike.api (whose require-closure holds datahike.query) and 1,601 some datahike namespace, so a namespace-grain reach reruns ~1,574 for a one-file Datahike change (today: 1,365 of 2,106, run22), and a form-grain reach of the ~5,000 library forms costs ~2.5x Seon's graph, whose full build already allocates ~1 GB. Rejected both.\n\nWhat exists [read]: a green records the functions its run called (seon.profile/reads, seon.proofs/reads-key) and is reused while each read keeps its digest (seon.proofs/read-digests); library vars have no form in the program db, so they carry no digest, and a pin moves every test through :env (seon.fx/inputs). Jolt keys each compiled form by the digest of its emitted text (eval-by-digest, the AOT cache's v1/forms).\n\nDesign: Jolt records at each definition the digest of the form that defined the var, (:jolt/digest (meta v)), answered by jolt.host/var-digest (deps). seon.profile/reads keeps library vars among the calls it records, and read-digests takes a library var's digest from var-digest as it takes a Seon var's from its form (tests-4). The Clojure libraries' pins then leave :env; Jolt's runtime and Chez stay in the binary's digest. A green whose recorded calls hold no changed library var is reused across a pin.\n\nEstimate: one string a var at definition (~70 bytes, ~20k vars: ~1.4 MB a process); a digest lookup per recorded library call at plan time, O(calls recorded); a pin reruns the tests that called a changed function [H: run22's change, the reads, query and cost tests, ~150]. Lower bound: the tests that executed a changed form.\n\nProof, red first: seon.proofs-test/a-green-is-reused-across-a-library-change-it-never-called: two greens, one calling a library function and one not; a change to that function's form reruns the first and reuses the second."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.proofs-test/a-green-is-reused-across-a-library-change-it-never-called}
  :seon.task/estimate {jolt.host/var-digest {:n 1, :order :constant, :ticks 200, :bytes 0}, seon.proofs/read-digests {:n 100, :order :linear, :ticks 20000, :bytes 4096}}}
